                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed90d11e-f88a-43f7-9b4d-1af65ea7c524",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb9a5b44-6e51-3b03-9cb3-d18507a7e84e",
                        "source_sense_id": "28acedd3-df5b-392e-8025-9114c1aadef4",
                        "source_sense_description": "een paal op een plein, waaraan mensen bij wijze van straf werden vastgemaakt om vernederd...",
                        "target_lang_word": "pillory",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pillory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fd1b68c-a538-3056-8a8c-999b9a0ab43e",
                                        "entry_id": "57de62a4-243a-3fdc-949d-bb6efaf728fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A framework on a post, with holes for the hands and head, used as a means of punishment and humiliation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "644f35af-f4cf-4e6f-a749-1355f4ed4b59",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd1b68c-a538-3056-8a8c-999b9a0ab43e",
                                                "text": "Maires and Maceris that meanes be betwene / The Kynge and the comon to kepe the lawes / To pũnyſhen on pyleries and pynning ſtoles / Bruſterrs and bakeſters, bochers and cokes / For theſe ar mẽ on this mold þᵉ moſt harme worketh / To the pore people that percel mele byghe[...]",
                                                "translation": "Mayors and mace-bearers, the means are between / The king and the commons to see the law kept, / To punish on pillories and punishment stools / Brewers and bakers, butchers and cooks, / For these are this world's men that work the most harm / To the poor people that must buy piece-meal.",
                                                "english": "Mayors and mace-bearers, the means are between / The king and the commons to see the law kept, / To punish on pillories and punishment stools / Brewers and bakers, butchers and cooks, / For these are this world's men that work the most harm / To the poor people that must buy piece-meal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f31f9710-da0d-45ab-99fb-fb38a4eb47a8",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd1b68c-a538-3056-8a8c-999b9a0ab43e",
                                                "text": "Cros·! þou dost no trouþe ; / On a pillori· my fruit to pinne, / He haþ no spot· of Adam sinne ; / Flesch· and veines· nou fleo a-twinne, / Wherfore I· rede of routhe·:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fa5fb25-ba8b-41e4-bb48-98ff7a0046c2",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd1b68c-a538-3056-8a8c-999b9a0ab43e",
                                                "text": "The other replied, That for ought they could ſee, the men were quiet, and ſober, and intended no body any harm ; and that there were many that Traded in their fair, that were more worthy to be put into the Cage, yea, and the Pillory too, then were the men that they had abuſed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pillory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e103550f-f051-3b7c-8576-8e26d4e3f8b0",
                                        "entry_id": "6b165dcc-b666-3f07-a7ed-13473e162aab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put in a pillory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03e04f5c-8c6c-32b2-9834-3777cade7082",
                                        "entry_id": "6b165dcc-b666-3f07-a7ed-13473e162aab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To subject to humiliation, scorn, ridicule or abuse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbe962df-8344-43c7-8f39-0c731f0528c9",
                                                "sense_id": "03e04f5c-8c6c-32b2-9834-3777cade7082",
                                                "text": "Mike Sarne would end up making a celluloid disasterpiece that is to this day pilloried as one of the worst films ever made."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6cf7978-eabe-3c21-aa56-3bccb0dd7b85",
                                        "entry_id": "6b165dcc-b666-3f07-a7ed-13473e162aab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To criticize harshly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92733bdf-ded8-4d56-b190-75aff2634c04",
                                                "sense_id": "e6cf7978-eabe-3c21-aa56-3bccb0dd7b85",
                                                "text": "The breakthrough came through Torres who, pilloried for his miss against Manchester United a week earlier, scored his second goal of the season."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19bf5632-0ad9-4869-b562-e9c0c9312367",
                                                "sense_id": "e6cf7978-eabe-3c21-aa56-3bccb0dd7b85",
                                                "text": "[T]o suggest that their mere acquaintance in any way undermines Pinker’s work would be to make the kind of ad hominem fallacy that he rightfully pillories in this book."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "53e5b999-c37e-4bf3-a974-c2c97afc02e7",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb9a5b44-6e51-3b03-9cb3-d18507a7e84e",
